        "phase": "No longer a missing-decoder gap on the SaftyFW side -- link_task.c decodes LINK_FRAME_REQUEST_ENABLE_CMD (0x02) today and relay_owner_command_energize() has its first caller. The remaining gap is on this side of the fence: no scenario issues the operator enable. firmware/SimFW/tools/virtual_dut/dut_core/main.c already accepts an ENABLE command mirroring relay_owner's TRIPPED-refuses / GRACE-defers / ARMED-honours behavior; run_dut_scenarios.py never sends one, because deciding WHEN a scenario would issue it is a scenario-library design question, not something a harness should invent. Owned by SimFW's scenario library, not by SaftyFW."
